## Context

[The #4471 review](/kb/incidents/4471-review/) shows that matching subjects can
hide separate faults. Different subjects can describe the same fault.
The executable dedupe component already compares causes while the written rule
still compares subjects.

## Proposal

Replace decision 0001 only after the support desk accepts this new record.
Keep the accepted original unchanged for the audit trail.

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID before counting.
2. Resolve the tenant's locale, booking form and input channel.
3. Compare the failure mechanism and reproduction evidence, not just the subject.
4. Merge only when the cause is established as the same.
5. Keep unknown tenants and uncertain symptoms in triage until investigated.
6. Rebuild computed views after new exports. Review stale prose against those views.

## Consequences

The desk must inspect evidence before merging. This costs more triage time but
keeps separate faults visible to engineering. Intake tags and computed classifications
are useful leads, not proof that every report has the same reproduced root cause.

